            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Taste the Fun"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I have tried the recipe at my home. It was very tasty and yummy. I loved the recipe. Thanks for sharing.",
            "datePublished": "2020-10-17T10:11:05.187Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Pallab Gupta"
            },
            "reviewBody": "For those who could not find \"black cumin\" - it's not cumin and is a literal translation of the Bengali or Hindi name. It's sold under the name \"kalonji\" or \"onion seeds\" - any Indian grocery store will carry it.\nAlso it's not accurate to say that only the leftover pieces are used for curry. As a die-hard Bengali with roots in both Bengals, I remember the best curry made out of fresh Katla (Buffalo)/ Rui (Rehu or Carp) and Bhetki. Every slice was used.",
            "datePublished": "2018-02-14T17:21:26.243Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "GuitarChef"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Also made this minus the black cumin. Came out wonderful.Flavorful without being 'hot'. If most Indian food is too spicy for you then this would be a good addition to your recipe box.Think I'll try it with salmon next time.",
            "datePublished": "2013-05-18T09:33:59.340Z"
          }
